<Base title="Colophon" description="How this site is built and who it borrows from.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>How this is built, and who it borrows from.</h1>
  </header>
  <article class="prose">
    <p>Astro, content collections, MDX. Static output, deployed on Vercel. Newsreader for the serif, Instrument Sans for everything else. The only colour on the site is the four domain tags, and each one means something.</p>
    <h2>The globe</h2>
    <p>The globe is <a href="https://github.com/shuding/cobe">cobe</a> by Shu Ding. The idea of having a globe at all is borrowed from <a href="https://fabianschultz.com">Fabian Schultz</a>, whose site source is <a href="https://github.com/fabe/site">public</a>.</p>
    <h2>The drum</h2>
    <p>Placeholder. The drumhead maths, and why a tabla can carry a pitch when most drums cannot, goes here once the drum piece is built.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
